From: somestupidgirl <sunnevanattsol@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kext_tools: signposts without the private libtrace header

signposts.h includes <os/signpost_private.h>, which Apple publish in no
SDK or source release, beside the public <os/signpost.h>.  Everything
kext_tools calls -- os_signpost_event_emit, the interval begin and end
macros, os_signpost_id_generate and _make_with_pointer -- is in the
public header, so the private one is included only where it exists.

--- a/signposts.h	2026-09-15 00:14:08
+++ b/signposts.h	2026-09-15 00:14:08
@@ -8,7 +8,9 @@
 
 #include <os/log.h>
 #include <os/signpost.h>
+#if __has_include(<os/signpost_private.h>)
 #include <os/signpost_private.h>
+#endif
 
 // shared events
 #define SIGNPOST_EVENT_BOOTCACHE_UPDATE_REASON  "BootcacheUpdateReason"
